# Workspace hygiene -- the clone must always be clean

`py -3 tools/repo_hygiene.py status|fix|stop-gate` is the enforcer; this rule is its pointer (ADR 051). The law: `AGENTS.md` §5.1 item 8.

1. **Never `git stash`.** Commit `wip:` on your branch instead; a stash used to prove a failure is pre-existing is popped the same turn.
2. **One worktree per task**, from `origin/master`, removed when the task ends. Never edit the main checkout from a worktree session.
3. **Stage explicit paths.** Never `git add -A` / `git add .`.
4. **Finish = clean.** Tree clean, branch pushed, PR open, worktree removed, `repo_hygiene.py status` OK. The Claude Code Stop hook (`stop-gate`) refuses the first dirty stop; if the user asked you to stop there, stop again and say why.
5. **After merge**, `repo_hygiene.py fix` reclaims the safe class only (merged branches contained in master, clean finished worktrees idle >24h, orphan remote refs). Stashes, dirty files and branches without a PR are reported, never auto-removed. Unmerged or squash-only tips: `branch-cleanup.mdc`. Scheduled-task exit codes: `maintenance-finish.mdc`.
